            0.088,
            0.816,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "3. Write the numerical value of each of the following: (i) $2 \\times 1 0 ^ { 3 }$ (ii) $7 ^ { 2 } \\times 2 ^ { 3 }$ (iii) $3 \\times 4 ^ { 4 }$ (iv) $( - 3 ) ^ { 2 } \\times ( - 5 ) ^ { 2 }$ (v) $3 ^ { 2 } \\times 1 0 ^ { 4 }$ (vi) $( - 2 ) ^ { 5 } \\times ( - 1 0 ) ^ { 6 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.156,
            0.691,
            0.213
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (i) 2000 (ii) 392 (iii) 768 (iv) 225 (v) 90000 (vi) –32000000"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.233,
            0.276,
            0.253
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 24"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.261,
            0.707,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": "3<sup>7</sup> can also be written as $3 ^ { 2 } \\times 3 ^ { 5 }$ . Can you reason out why? Ans: $3 ^ { 7 } = 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 3$ $= ( 3 \\times 3 ) \\times ( 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 )$ = 3<sup>2</sup> × 3<sup>5</sup>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.371,
            0.606,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": "？ Use this observation to compute the following. (i) $2 ^ { 9 }$ (ii) $5 ^ { 7 }$ (iii) $4 ^ { 6 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.417,
            0.519,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (i) One of the ways is $2^{9}=2^{4}\\times 2^{5}=16\\times 32=512$ (ii) One of the ways is $5^{7}=5^{3}\\times 5^{4}=125\\times 625=78125$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.52,
            0.845,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "？ Write the following expressions as a power of a power in at least two different ways: (i) $8 ^ { 6 }$ (ii) $7 ^ { 1 5 }$ (iii) $9 ^ { 1 4 }$ (iv) $5 ^ { 8 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.582,
            0.445,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** (i) $8 ^ { 6 }   = ( 8 ^ { 2 } ) ^ { 3 }$ $8 ^ { 6 }   =   ( 2 ^ { 3 } ) ^ { 6 }   =   2 ^ { 1 8 }$ (ii) $7 ^ { 1 5 }   =   ( 7 ^ { 3 } ) ^ { 5 } \\; ; \\qquad 7 ^ { 1 5 }   =   \\overline { { ( 7 ^ { 5 } ) ^ { 3 } } }$ (iii) $9 ^ { 1 4 }   = ( 9 ^ { 2 } ) ^ { 7 }$ $9^{14} = (3^2)^{14} = 3^{28}$ (iv) $5 ^ { 8 }   = ( 5 ^ { 2 } ) ^ { 4 }$ $5 ^ { 8 }   = ( 5 ^ { 4 } ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.752,
            0.276,
            0.772
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 25"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.779,
            0.847,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": "？ Write the number of lotuses (in exponential form) when the pond was — (i) fully covered (ii) half covered **Ans:** (i) $2 ^ { 3 0 }$ (ii) $2 ^ { 2 9 }$"
        },
        {
